              "kind": "external",
              "justification": "The finding incorrectly flags '{ % crsf_token % }' as a CSRF bypass, but this is a typographical error in the template: the correct Django template tag is '{% csrf_token %}' (without spaces). The malformed tag will simply render as plain text and fail to emit the CSRF token, which means the control is effectively absent \u2014 but the tool's claim of a 'CSRF bypass' misattributes the cause. The actual issue is a broken implementation of the CSRF control, not a bypass of an existing one. Since the control is not properly implemented (not bypassed), the finding's assertion is factually incorrect."
