              "reasoning": "The finding flags a potential Reflected XSS at {{ error_flash(error=error) }}, but error_flash is a custom Jinja2 macro imported from components/forms.html. In Flask-Jinja2 templates, output is automatically escaped by default unless explicitly disabled (e.g., | safe or Markup()). The macro name 'error_flash' suggests it renders user-facing error messages, which are typically generated server-side from flashed messages (e.g., flash('error', 'message') in Python), not directly from request parameters. Even if the error value originates from user input, Jinja2's autoescaping would neutralize XSS unless autoescape=False is set globally \u2014 which is not shown here. The tool misattributes the risk to the template line, but the actual mitigation (autoescaping) is a framework default that applies unless disabled, and no disabling flag is visible. Thus, the asserted XSS risk does not hold in this context.",
